# Rebuild yourself

After changing kernel, apps, host tools that affect the guest, or anything the user needs to run next — **rebuild and stage artifacts yourself**. Do not leave `argon build` / `mkaxe` / copy-into-share as “you should run…”.

## Paths (canonical)

| What | Path |
|---|---|
| App / driver images (archive) | `build/apps/` (`.AXE`, `.SYS`) |
| HostFS / sync share | `build/sd_card/` |

`tools/mkaxe.py` **always** copies the built image into both directories after a
successful write (unless `--no-stage`). Prefer `-o build/apps/NAME.AXE`.

## Typical

- Firmware: `argon build` (or `argon check` when tests are warranted)
- Apps: `python tools/mkaxe.py … -o build/apps/FOO.AXE …` (auto-stages to `build/sd_card/` too)
- Run QEMU with HostFS: `argon run -Gfx -HostFs build\sd_card` (or `-Share build\sd_card`)
- Report what you rebuilt and any command that failed

Only skip a rebuild when the change is docs-only or the user explicitly says not to build.
